- `UserDetailsService` — реализация, которая берёт `User` из репозитория и маппит в `org.springframework.security.core.userdetails.User` (или свой `CustomUserDetails`).

## 5. Конфигурация Spring Security
- `SecurityFilterChain` (Spring Security 6+):
  - `/auth/**` и `/register` — permitAll
  - остальное — authenticated
- `PasswordEncoder` — `BCryptPasswordEncoder`
- `AuthenticationManager` — через `AuthenticationConfiguration`
- Для API: stateless + JWT-фильтр; для MVC: formLogin/session

## 6. Связка в коде (ключевой пример)

```java
@Entity
public class User {
    @Id @GeneratedValue private Long id;
    @Column(unique = true, nullable = false) private String username;
    private String password;
    @ElementCollection(fetch = FetchType.EAGER)
    private Set<String> roles = new HashSet<>();
    // getters/setters
}

public interface UserRepository extends JpaRepository<User, Long> {
    Optional<User> findByUsername(String username);
}

@Service
public class DbUserDetailsService implements UserDetailsService {
    private final UserRepository repo;
    public DbUserDetailsService(UserRepository repo) { this.repo = repo; }

    @Override
    public UserDetails loadUserByUsername(String username) {
        User u = repo.findByUsername(username)
            .orElseThrow(() -> new UsernameNotFoundException(username));
        return org.springframework.security.core.userdetails.User
            .withUsername(u.getUsername())
            .password(u.getPassword())
            .authorities(u.getRoles().stream()
                .map(r -> new SimpleGrantedAuthority("ROLE_" + r)).toList())
            .build();
    }
}

@Configuration
@EnableWebSecurity
public class SecurityConfig {
    @Bean
    SecurityFilterChain filterChain(HttpSecurity http) throws Exception {
        http
          .csrf(csrf -> csrf.disable())
          .authorizeHttpRequests(a -> a
              .requestMatchers("/auth/**", "/register").permitAll()
              .anyRequest().authenticated())
          .httpBasic(Customizer.withDefaults());
        return http.build();
    }

    @Bean PasswordEncoder passwordEncoder() { return new BCryptPasswordEncoder(); }

    @Bean AuthenticationManager authManager(AuthenticationConfiguration cfg) throws Exception {
        return cfg.getAuthenticationManager();
    }
}
```

